<!--
    USB-REDIRECT FEATURE (Part 1/3): deliberately empty — a <resources> with
    no <usb-device> children matches every attached USB device regardless of
    vendor/product/class. FreeRDP's URBDRC channel redirects any USB device
    class per MS-RDPEUSB §1.3 (see UsbDeviceClassCategory's doc comment in
    UsbModels.kt), so narrowing this filter to specific classes would only
    limit which devices can auto-launch UsbDeviceAttachedActivity while the
    app isn't already running — never which devices this feature actually
    supports redirecting once running. The user-facing "is this device
    actually redirected" gate is the approval flow in
    UsbRedirectionSettingsScreen, not this filter.

    Kept as a SEPARATE resource from usb_device_filter.xml (the pre-existing
    SMARTCARD-REDIRECT FEATURE filter, narrowed to interface class 0x0B and
    referenced from RdpSessionActivity's own USB_DEVICE_ATTACHED meta-data)
    rather than widening that one — RdpSessionActivity's narrow smart-card-
    only filter is intentional (see its own manifest comment) and must keep
    working exactly as before regardless of this feature.
-->
